 "notes": [
  "AWS: 34 commercial regions in the standard partition (docs AZ table) + eusc-de-east-1 (European Sovereign Cloud, GA 2026-01-14) + 2 GovCloud (excluded) + 2 China (partner_operated) = 39, matching the '39 Geographic Regions' on aws.amazon.com regions_az. Announced: Saudi Arabia, Chile.",
  "AWS us-east-1 is gaining a Maryland AZ ('Coming in 2026'); same country, no effect.",
  "Azure restricted-access regions (australiacentral2, brazilsoutheast, francesouth, germanynorth, norwaywest, southafricawest, switzerlandwest, uaecentral) are listed but only matter where a GA region already exists, so no country status depends on them.",
  "Azure Taiwan North carries a preview/coming-soon marker on the regions list; coded announced, not ga.",
  "Azure Government, US Sec, and legacy Germany sovereign regions excluded. Azure Extended Zones, AWS Local Zones/Outposts/Wavelength, and CDN PoPs excluded.",
  "GCP: 43 regions per cloud.google.com/about/locations (page updated 2026-10-05); the Memorystore regions page lists exactly 43, used as the per-region list. The full compute regions-zones page was too long to read in one fetch. Countries are inferred from city names on that page.",
  "GCP announced regions still not live as of this check: Austria, Greece, Norway (all announced 2022), Malaysia and New Zealand (2022/2023), Kuwait (2023). The current GCP locations page does not show 'upcoming' text in fetched form, so announced status rests on older announcements plus their absence from the live list; any of them may have been cancelled quietly.",
  "Azure announced list (Finland, Greece, Saudi Arabia, Taiwan, Thailand, East US 3) comes from azurespeed.com (S5, third-party) and is corroborated by Microsoft's geographies page (S1), which lumps 'available or coming soon' together.",
  "Azure Kenya (with G42, 2024) and Kuwait (2025) are announced by Microsoft (S1 press release) but appear on no current Microsoft region list; status low-confidence.",
